 163 /// Verifies the release roster a merged release commit claims, against a
 164 /// release-decision file committed alongside it at `decision_path`.
 165 ///
 166 /// This is intentionally *not* a second computation of changeset, fixed-group,
 167 /// linked-group, cascade, or pre-release-policy inclusion. `plan_version`
 168 /// (via [`derive_release_decision`]) already computed that once, correctly,
 169 /// when the release PR was generated -- and `callisto version --emit-decision`
 170 /// commits its exact output alongside the manifest and changelog edits.
 171 /// Re-deriving that policy a second time here, from raw git diffs, is exactly
 172 /// the kind of duplicated logic that drifts: an earlier version of this
 173 /// function did just that, understood only a direct changeset match, and
 174 /// rejected every real release in this repository once a fixed-group cascade
 175 /// (a case its reimplementation never learned) touched an unnamed sibling.
 176 ///
 177 /// Instead, this function reads the committed decision back and confirms the
 178 /// commit's actual diff matches it exactly -- no more, no less.
 179 /// [`ReleaseDecisionV1`]'s own deserializer already rejects a decision whose
 180 /// entries don't match its content digest, so a hand-edited or corrupted
 181 /// decision file fails before this function's own diff cross-check runs.
 182 ///
 183 /// The caller must check out the exact merge commit in detached HEAD state
 184 /// before creating an intent. GitHub-specific PR/approval provenance belongs
